<p>Feedback on this was kinda divided in chat, but hey, here goes. Many, many thanks to Dmatix, Drewbear, Burns, and MisterFlames for looking over the initial draft, Scantron and Mann for going over the next edited version, and Woggle, Teedles, Kens, and SRegan for helping me with the more in-depth edits. Also Silber and Roget for giving it the final look over. If I forgot someone, my apologies. D: I’ve hit a bit of an inspiration slump lately, so I do appreciate all the help.</p>
<p>Edit: OMG AZZLEFLUX I AM SO SORRY. D: Thank you for helping me prevent this from becoming too much like my other articles.</p>
<p>Scantron found the picture for me. Thanks, Scanny! <strong>ETA:</strong> since I can't find the source for the image, I have replaced it with a wikimedia commons picture that's Public Domain: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.MOLL.342114_-_Sinum_perspectivum_(Say,_1831)_-_Naticidae_-_Mollusc_shell.jpeg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.MOLL.342114_-_Sinum_perspectivum_(Say,_1831)_-_Naticidae_-_Mollusc_shell.jpeg</a></p>
<p>Anyway, I first thought this up when I remembered something from my childhood: apparently one way to keep a secret is to whisper it into a seashell, then throw the shell into a body of water.</p>
<p>I tried to focus on the fact that the Foundation inherently holds an incredible amount of influence on the world through the SCP objects it contains, and fairly often in the attempt to learn more about the skips, they end up sacrificing their own people.</p>

